@ 32.1.2 - Proto-Chatino to Tataltepec Chatino
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Upson, B.W., and Robert E. Longacre (1965), “Proto-Chatino Phonology”. International Journal of American Linguistics 31(4):312 – 322
	t > tʲ / _õ (…again…lolwut)
	t > t͡ʃ / #_iç
	tʲ > t͡ʃ / _i:[-long -stress]
	tʲ > t / _a
	kʲ > tʲ
	c > t͡ʃ / i_
	t͡ʃ > c
	s > ʃ / [+front]_ (? Not a lot of data available on this one)
	ʃ > s
	{ l, n } > { lʲ, nʲ } / e_ in %:[-long -stress]
	ç > ʔ (? Not sure if I’m reading the phone(me)s right on this one)
	e > a / _ʔ in %:[-stress]
	{ et, el, en } > { itʲ, elʲ, enʲ }
	e > i / _j
	ɛ > ı̃ / S_#
	ɛ > i / n_#
	ɛ > e / _ʔ#, in monosyllables